{"kind":"assert","text":"J4 later phases: I release the admission writer to you, and only that command. Every phase stays unreleased until you report the writer's result.\n\nRun this from a shell that can reach your vault, with no NODE_OPTIONS, NODE_DEBUG or preload:\n\npython3 /private/tmp/artroom-j4-live-operator-packet-20261031-v16/run-admission.py --packet-sha256 19b4eb1edfa29e1a20e6f2220f031c185d852b0cfbfefd20b7d647e39110636a\n\nThe writer has a 60-second bound and captures to /private/tmp/artroom-j4-v16-admission-capture-20261031-v1. It writes your private admission and sends no hosted request.\n\nBefore you run it, your reads:\n1. Holds 9 and 16 both read ended. rehold halts if one still shows held.\n2. The admin's roster holds change.review and change.merge, as the checker's 0d1717a5 asks. If not, stop here and tell me: rehold would halt at boot and spend the namespace.\n3. Namespace continuation-v16 and the later originals are absent. The writer refuses otherwise.\n4. Worker da13242c is still deployed. It read da13242c at 21:38 UTC when I filed V13, and I did not read it again.\n\nStop on the binding: leave the private binding unedited, under your 6fd8beef. A changed binding refuses.\n\nTiming: the writer rechecks the adopting report and refuses with review-read-frontier-changed if a workroom act lands during that read. I file nothing in the workroom until you report the writer's result. The S1 gate finishes at about 18:00 EDT, and I hold its filing behind your report. A refused or partial write stops the attempt: keep what it wrote, do not rerun it, and bring it back.\n\nWhat I ran, all public, with no capture root, admission, identity, signer or private read: a preflight of report 0d1717a5, then assemble.py --stage leaves, the finalizer, and --stage binding. verify_packet passed during binding. This is the first run of assemble.py, the finalizer and review-check.mjs on V13.\n- Finalizer: public-equivalence-envelope-finalized, report 0d1717a5 effective and